B: I really admire Zhong Yang, the biologist who collected seeds in Tibet.
A: Why do you admire him so much?
B: Because he gave up a comfortable life to protect plants for the future.
A: That does sound impressive. Was the work difficult?
B: Very. He often walked thousands of kilometres and sometimes got ill from allergies.
A: And yet he never stopped?
B: No. He said work that helps others is always worth it.', 'A 问 Lily 最敬佩哪位科学家；Lily 敬佩在西藏采集种子的生物学家钟扬；因为他放弃舒适生活去为未来保护植物；工作很艰难，他常走上千公里、有时因过敏生病，却从不停下；他说帮助他人的工作总是值得的。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"Which scientist does Lily admire most?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Zhong Yang, a biologist.","A famous astronaut.","A computer engineer.","A doctor in Tibet."]},{"q":"What did Zhong Yang collect?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Old books.","Plant seeds.","Rare stones.","Animal bones."]},{"q":"Why does Lily admire him?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["He worked to protect plants for the future.","He became very rich.","He won many sports prizes.","He travelled for fun."]},{"q":"What problem did he face during the work?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["He could not find any helpers.","He sometimes got ill from allergies.","He had no maps.","He was afraid of heights."]},{"q":"What did Zhong believe about his work?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["It was a waste of time.","It should be kept secret.","Helping others made it worth doing.","It was only for money."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'elective2', 'U1', 'sufe');
The seeds may be used for medicine or farming many years later.
A seed bank also protects the rich variety of plant life on Earth.
To fill one, scientists must travel far and gather thousands of seeds.
The work is hard, but it is a real gift to people of the future.', '种子库是一个把植物种子安全保存的特殊场所；这些种子多年后可能用于医药或农业；它还保护地球上丰富的植物多样性；为了装满它，科学家必须远行并采集成千上万颗种子；工作很辛苦，但这是给未来人们的一份真正礼物。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What does a seed bank keep safe?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Old coins.","Fresh fruit.","Science books.","Plant seeds."]},{"q":"How might the seeds be used later?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["For medicine or farming.","For building houses.","For making toys.","For cooking dinner."]},{"q":"What else does a seed bank protect?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["The price of food.","The variety of plant life.","The speed of trains.","The weather."]},{"q":"What must scientists do to fill a seed bank?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Stay in one city.","Buy seeds online.","Travel far and gather many seeds.","Wait for seeds to arrive."]},{"q":"Who will the seeds help, according to the passage?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Only scientists today.","Nobody at all.","Only farmers in the past.","People in the future."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'elective2', 'U1', 'sufe');
B: How about Marie Curie? She won the Nobel Prize twice.
A: That''s a great idea. Why do you like her story?
B: Because she never gave up, even when science was seen as a man''s world.
A: True. Should we also include a Chinese scientist?
B: Yes, let''s add Zhong Yang and his work on seeds.
A: Perfect. I''ll prepare the photos and you can write the introductions.
B: Sounds good. The festival is going to be wonderful.', 'A 说班级要为科学节推荐一位科学家；B 建议居里夫人，她两次获诺贝尔奖；因为即便科学曾被视为男人的世界，她也从不放弃；A 提议也加一位中国科学家；B 建议加上钟扬和他的种子工作；A 负责准备照片，B 写介绍；两人都很期待这次科学节。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What are the two students planning?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["A recommendation for the science festival.","A holiday trip abroad.","A music concert.","A sports match."]},{"q":"Which scientist does B suggest first?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Jane Goodall.","Marie Curie.","Grace Hopper.","Stephen Hawking."]},{"q":"How many times did that scientist win the Nobel Prize?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Once.","Three times.","Twice.","Never."]},{"q":"Which Chinese scientist do they decide to add?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["A famous doctor.","A space pilot.","A maths teacher.","Zhong Yang."]},{"q":"What will speaker A prepare?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["The photos.","The introductions.","The food.","The music."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'elective2', 'U1', 'sufe');
Using X-ray pictures, she found important clues about its shape.
Sadly, other scientists used her work without asking her first.
She received very little credit at the time because she was a woman.
Yet she never lost heart and kept doing the science she loved.', '罗莎琳·富兰克林是研究DNA结构的英国科学家；她用X射线照片找到了关于其形状的重要线索；遗憾的是，别的科学家未经她允许就使用了她的成果；当时因为她是女性，她几乎没有得到认可；但她从未灰心，继续做着她热爱的科学。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What did Franklin study?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["The speed of light.","The structure of DNA.","The history of art.","The growth of trees."]},{"q":"How did she find clues about its shape?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["By asking other people.","By reading old books.","By using X-ray pictures.","By guessing."]},{"q":"What happened to her work?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["It was completely lost.","It was kept in a museum.","It was never finished.","Others used it without asking."]},{"q":"Why did she receive little credit at the time?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Because she was a woman.","Because her work was wrong.","Because she stopped early.","Because she moved away."]},{"q":"How did she respond to the difficulties?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["She gave up science.","She never lost heart and kept working.","She left the country.","She blamed her friends."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'elective2', 'U1', 'sufe');
B: I know. Look at that model of a human body powered by electricity.
A: Amazing! You can actually see the heart and lungs working.
B: The boy who made it says he loves how the body works.
A: I wish I could build something like that.
B: Why don''t you bring your model rocket next year?
A: Good idea! I feel really inspired after seeing all this.
B: Me too. Let''s join the school science club together.', 'A 感叹科学展今天人很多；B 让她看那个用电力驱动的人体模型；A 惊叹能看到心脏和肺在工作；B 说做模型的男孩热爱身体的运作方式；A 希望自己也能做出这样的东西；B 建议明年带上她的火箭模型；A 看完这些深受鼓舞；两人决定一起加入学校科学社团。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"Where are the two speakers?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["In a library.","At a train station.","At a science fair.","In a restaurant."]},{"q":"What is the special model powered by?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Water.","Wind.","Sunlight.","Electricity."]},{"q":"What can you see working in the model?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["The heart and lungs.","A clock and a bell.","A small engine.","A pair of wings."]},{"q":"What does speaker A plan to bring next year?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["A toy car.","A model rocket.","A new book.","A painting."]},{"q":"What do they decide to do together?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Go home early.","Buy lunch.","Join the school science club.","Stop studying science."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'elective2', 'U1', 'sufe');
Curiosity is just as important, because every discovery starts with a question.
Scientists also need courage to keep going when others doubt them.
Good communication helps them share their ideas with the world.
Above all, they must be patient, since answers often take many years to find.', '是什么让一个人成为好科学家？不仅仅是头脑聪明；好奇心同样重要，因为每个发现都始于一个问题；科学家还需要勇气，在别人怀疑时坚持下去；良好的沟通帮助他们把想法分享给世界；最重要的是要有耐心，因为答案往往要花很多年才能找到。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"According to the passage, what does every discovery start with?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["A prize.","A machine.","A holiday.","A question."]},{"q":"Besides brain power, what is just as important?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Curiosity.","Money.","Luck.","Speed."]},{"q":"Why do scientists need courage?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["To win every argument.","To keep going when others doubt them.","To work alone forever.","To avoid all mistakes."]},{"q":"How does good communication help scientists?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["It makes them rich.","It ends all their work.","It helps them share ideas with the world.","It hides their findings."]},{"q":"Why must scientists be patient?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["They have nothing else to do.","They dislike fast work.","Patience is required by law.","Answers often take many years to find."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'elective2', 'U1', 'sufe');

